  "rationales": {"U":"'The requirement shall be respected in every ETCS application' lacks subject clarity and domain context; 'respected' is vague and non-technical, failing to convey actionable behavior — evidence: 'shall be respected'; this violates ISO/IEC/IEEE 29148 understandability criteria for stakeholder-oriented language.","A":"'Every ETCS application' is ambiguous without defining scope boundaries (e.g., Baseline 3 vs. Baseline 4, Class A vs. Class B), and 'respected' admits multiple interpretations (implemented? verified? declared?); evidence: 'every ETCS application' and 'shall be respected' — no normative reference or definition provided.","C":"The statement is plausibly correct as a policy intent but lacks traceability to an authoritative source (e.g., SRS-ETCS v3.6.0 §4.2.1 or SUBSET-026); absence of citation reduces confidence in correctness — evidence: no reference to standard, baseline, or clause.","V":"No testable condition or observable outcome is specified; 'shall be respected' cannot be confirmed via inspection, analysis, or test — evidence: 'shall be respected' provides zero pass/fail criteria or measurable artifact."}, 
  "suggestions": {"U":"The system shall implement this requirement in all ETCS on-board and trackside applications conforming to ETCS Baseline 3 or later.","A":"The system shall implement this requirement in all ETCS on-board and trackside applications conforming to ETCS Baseline 3 or later.","C":"The system shall implement this requirement in all ETCS on-board and trackside applications conforming to ETCS Baseline 3 or later, as mandated by SUBSET-026 §5.3.2.","V":"For each ETCS on-board and trackside application conforming to Baseline 3 or later, the requirement shall be implemented such that the generated safety-related output includes a verifiable traceability tag 'R1' in the SRS-ETCS traceability matrix (column 'Implemented Requirement ID')."},
